Bank earning season is testing Canadian financials as TSX futures hold steady, giving dividend focused TFSA holders a window to reassess exposure. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 151. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:57.980
before putting real money to work. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,709, up 4 tenths of a percent. The NASDAQ composite reached 26,409, up 1.1%. The TSX composite finished at 36,704, down 3 tenths of a percent. Tech leadership on Invidia developments contrasts with Canadian bank results dominating attention on the TSX.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:24.340
The Fed's September decision remains uncertain according to recent commentary from former officials. Our simulated portfolio stands at a cumulative $305.98 across 56 trades, at a 54% win rate. The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ sits at plus 0.8% across 5 rules-based trades since the record began on August 18th, 2026.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:36.420
Earnings reports from growth names like robotics and mining developers offer a repeatable way to capture short-term alpha when results beat expectations on both revenue and project milestones.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:45.620
Today's filings from Kraken Robotics and several gold copper developers show how second quarter updates can shift sentiment quickly in small cap names.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:59.200
Screen for companies that pair positive earnings with concrete project catalysts such as equipment financing, letters of interest or lifted suspensions. Enter only if volume exceeds the 20-day average on the reaction day.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:06.680
This approach has historically worked best in the first 48 hours after release, before broader sector rotation takes over.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:20.060
Risk comes from low float names that gap and reverse on thin volume, so always set a hard stop at the pre-report low. Use your broker's earnings calendar filter plus volume scanner to surface candidates each quarter.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:31.880
Kraken Robotics filed its unaudited consolidated financial statements and management discussion and analysis for the three and six months ended June 30th, 2026 on Cedar Plus.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:41.860
Investors can cross-reference those documents directly with the company's project pipeline to gauge whether reported results translate into near-term cash visibility.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:49.320
The same filter applies to names releasing metallurgical test data or export credit support updates on the same day.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:59.020
This flash trade on Kraken Robotics demonstrates how to isolate an earnings catalyst from sector noise by requiring volume confirmation on the reaction day.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:11.700
The pick is png.v Kraken Robotics on the TSX Venture. The catalyst is the second quarter 2026 financial results filed with potential for positive project updates.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:17.660
Watch for volume above the 20-day average on the open with nearest resistance at recent highs.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:26.460
Thin float volatility could produce quick reversal, so the stop sits at the pre-release low and limits loss to roughly 8-10%.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:38.960
The target is plus 2% to plus 4% intraday if volume confirms. Confidence is medium because the earnings catalyst is live, but sector rotation into broader tech may cap follow through.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.820
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:50.320
Yesterday's weekly hold on TLG delivered a clear alpha outcome because volume state elevated through the entire window.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:58.120
The position entered at $2.05 on the Thursday open and exited at $2.31 on the Wednesday close.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:06.120
That produced a gain of 12.68% or $126.83 on a $1,000 position.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:16.140
Over the same six calendar day window the NASDAQ rose approximately 2.8%, so the trade generated 9.88% alpha versus the benchmark.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:21.680
The drilling extension 400 meters beyond the current resource pit shell drove the move.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:29.900
What this teaches us is that catalyst-driven names already in a sector rotation need volume above the 20-day average before entry.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:41.620
Upgrading from OTCQB to OTCQX gives Canadian issuers broader US investor visibility and tighter spreads without full NYSE listing costs.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:49.680
Investors gain easier access to names like astra exploration through standard US brokerage accounts once the upgrade is complete.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.180
Check your broker's international trading desk or OTC markets platform for eligibility.

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:06.020
The upgrade removes the previous OTCQB trading restrictions and places the company on the OTCQX best market which carries higher disclosure standards.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:15.020
Canadian investors holding the TSXV listing can now route US orders through the same account without needing a separate cross-border custodian.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:27.700
Third-party labs such as Capus, Cassidy and Associates run bottle roll tests that quantify recovery rates across different host rocks, directly informing feasibility studies and mind planning.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:36.080
Retail investors following junior developers can use these results to separate viable projects from conceptual ones before committing capital.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:42.360
Review the full test parameters in the company's press release rather than headline recovery percentages alone.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:52.840
Blossom Gold announced initial bottle roll test results from multiple host rock types and alteration styles from both oxidized and fresh rock at the Rosebud project.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:06:01.060
The test work program is designed to define recovery characteristics for the major host rocks ahead of mind planning and feasibility studies.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:11.400
The preventive suspension at Patagonia Gold's Argentine project has been lifted after an agreement on local worker hiring and training, allowing operations to resume.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.700
The company also announced the third Dore dispatched from the project.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:24.080
This removes an operational overhang that had previously halted certain activities at the flagship Calcutrio site in Rio Negro Province.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:31.620
Add PGDC.V to a watch list for volume confirmation on the first full day of resumed activity.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:43.420
Troyless announced a non-binding letter of interest for up to $132 million US dollars in export credit support from Finvera for Metso equipment at its Quebec Gold Copper project.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:50.000
The letter remains subject to final documentation and is tied to equipment procurement announced two days earlier.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:57.040
Monitor TLG.TO for sustained volume above the 20-day average before considering any new position.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:01.960
Raymond James raised its NVIDIA price target to $515.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:10.080
The new target implies a roughly $13 trillion market cap and reflects continued confidence in the AI infrastructure build out.

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:17.700
Trim any oversized NVDA exposure if the stock fails to hold above its 20-day moving average on the next pullback.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:25.200
TSX futures are holding near flat as investors digest Canadian bank results amid ongoing geopolitical tensions.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:32.180
Hold CAD cash in a TFSA until the bank earnings reaction clarifies sector rotation direction.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:38.040
The AI infrastructure trade continues to show leadership on the back of fresh NVIDIA developments,

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:43.660
which keeps the question of whether CapEx momentum persists squarely in focus for the weeks ahead.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:52.720
Imagine you bought shares in a TSXV mining name the morning after it reported second quarter results and a new equipment financing letter of interest.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.540
Your order filled at the open yet the stock faded by mid-day.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:06.440
What actually happened is that the headline numbers looked strong, but the letter of interest was non-binding, so institutions that had prepositions sold into the retail rush.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:12.840
Reported revenue or project progress moves the stock only when accompanied by binding cash flow visibility.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.540
Otherwise the initial pop is absorbed by earlier buyers locking in gains.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:27.380
Most retail investors skip the fine print on whether the catalyst is binding or aspirational and end up holding the bag after the first hour volume spike.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:40.040
The pro tip is to open the full management discussion and analysis within 30 minutes of the release and check for words like non-binding or subject to final documentation before adding to size.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:45.360
The concrete misconception to avoid is treating every positive headline as equal.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:54.620
The fix is to require at least one line item that converts directly into near-term cash or production before treating the reaction as confirmed.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:09:05.300
Troyless mining announced a non-binding letter of interest from Finvera for up to approximately $132 million in potential export credit support.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:16.400
The press release explicitly labels the letter as non-binding, which means any price reaction must be discounted until further documentation converts the support into a firm commitment.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:31.700
Patagonia Gold reported that a preventive, partial and temporary suspension at its Calcutro project in Argentina was lifted after an agreement with the Secretariat of Labor of the Province of Rio Negro on hiring and training local workers.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:39.620
That development carries more immediate operational weight because the suspension itself has been removed rather than merely proposed.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:52.100
Blossom Gold released initial bottle-rolled test results from multiple host rock types at its Rosebud Open Pit Heap Leach project in Nevada, with CAPAs, Cassidy and Associates conducting the program.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:10:02.880
Those test parameters appear in the release and can be reviewed line by line to assess recovery consistency across oxidized and fresh rock before any valuation adjustment.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:17.760
Astra Exploration qualified to trade on the OTCQX Best Market after upgrading from the OTCQB Venture Market, a step that improves US investor access without requiring a full NYSE listing.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:30.140
Open your brokerage platform, pull up the last three earnings releases for any TSXV name you own, and highlight every sentence containing non-binding, subject to or contingent on.

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:34.220
Count how many of those qualifiers appear in the most recent release.

